WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.181 --> 00:00:03.500
(enchanting music)

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.337
- [Aelita] Sometimes they say,

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.300
"Oh, a kid did it, it's
not worth anything."

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.130
Lots of people say that 12 year olds

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.080
are such an annoying age.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.430
Critics say that I'm like Jackson Pollock.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.230
And they say it as a compliment,

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:20.040
but I want to be known for my own style,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.923
not being compared to someone else.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.840
- [Narrator] This Great Big
Story was made possible by Lego,

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:29.977
play her way.

00:00:29.977 --> 00:00:33.144
(upbeat string music)

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:37.880
My name is Aelita Andre.
I'm an abstract painter.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.830
And I'm from Melbourne, Australia.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.160
- [Narrator] At only 12 years old,

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.373
Aelita has been in the
industry for over a decade.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.150
- [Aelita] I started painting
when I was nine months old.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.670
My dad put a canvas down on the floor

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.750
because he used to paint a little bit.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.010
I just started crawling on the canvas

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:59.420
and started painting before him (laughs).

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.320
That's how everything started,
that was my first painting.

00:01:05.673 --> 00:01:07.430
(charming music)

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:11.490
My first show was at the
age of two years old.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.890
- [Narrator] Without telling
the gallery owner her age,

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.560
her mother presented the work

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.120
and Aelita was booked for her first show.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.200
Since then, she has taken
her art across the globe

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.040
and has sold paintings for
around $35,000 U.S. dollars.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:30.480
I've been to London,
Russia, Japan, New York,

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.688
Italy, China, mom, where else?

00:01:33.688 --> 00:01:34.521
- [Mom] Hong Kong.

00:01:34.521 --> 00:01:35.920
Hong Kong, but--
Four times.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.137
Four times (laughs).

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:43.930
I paint every few days, but
mainly when I'm inspired.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:46.890
When I paint, I usually
think about the universe,

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.910
I think about animals,

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:51.463
pretty much everything
that has to do with nature.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.820
With the violins on the canvas,

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:59.483
I want to show that the
whole universe is singing.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.760
- [Narrator] Although Aelita's young,

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.840
she understands the harsh
critics in the art world.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.120
- [Aelita] When people question my talent,

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.670
usually I don't mind because I think

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:12.510
that everyone should
have their own opinion.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:13.840
- [Narrator] But there is one critic

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.830
whose opinion does matter.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.850
So Fluffy is our little pet art critic.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.910
He usually starts biting me

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.970
or biting the painting
if he doesn't like it.

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:25.600
But it will be great.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.070
- [Aelita] My mom and
dad encouraged my art

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:29.688
and I'm so happy.

00:02:29.688 --> 00:02:30.521
(Aelita and dad laughing)

00:02:30.521 --> 00:02:32.620
So I definitely think that I'm going to

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.310
be doing painting for the rest of my life.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:37.413
It's something that I love so much.

00:02:42.122 --> 00:02:45.205
(electronic chiming)

